{
  "id": 475292739,
  "iid": 24449,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "wslua_tree: check types in TreeItem:add before adding",
  "description": "Perform an explicit check that the passed-in value for\n`TreeItem_add_any()` (ie, `TreeItem:add[_le]()`) matches the type of the\nfield for which it's being added. Use `THROW_LUA_ERROR()` if not.\n\nNeeded because both epan/libwireshark and Lua use `setjmp/longjmp` for\nexception handling, but bad things happen if a Lua exception jumps out\nof an epan try block. [Fuller explanation\nhere.](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/work_items/21075#note_3256905474)\n\nAI-Assisted: no\n\nCloses #21075",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-04-18T14:51:55.921Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-28T13:13:42.076Z",
